{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116190",
      "title": "Going Zoneless!",
      "lectureOrder": 207,
      "videoOrder": 198,
      "sourceHash": "613a3e146b42529fa51622fd35f99d9fb76a55bdfdb0cf3f61f380df2b3968d3",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.75,
          "end": 3.15,
          "en": "So you did learn a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.15,
          "end": 6.12,
          "en": "about Angulars change detection mechanism,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.12,
          "end": 9.36,
          "en": "but at its core, everything you learned here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.36,
          "end": 13.68,
          "en": "pretty much everything, still only works the way it does",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.68,
          "end": 18.68,
          "en": "because Angular uses zone.js because it's that zone",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.59,
          "end": 22.92,
          "en": "that wraps the Angular app kind of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.92,
          "end": 26.22,
          "en": "that tells Angular when an event occurs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.22,
          "end": 31.22,
          "en": "or once something changed and that in the end is the source",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 31.95,
          "end": 33.99,
          "en": "for the change detection or",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 33.99,
          "end": 36.785,
          "en": "for most change detection cycles here, no matter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.785,
          "end": 41.19,
          "en": "if you're using a service or signals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 41.19,
          "end": 46.05,
          "en": "but if you are using signals like here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 46.05,
          "end": 48.36,
          "en": "in the counter.component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 48.36,
          "end": 52.492,
          "en": "then you can actually get rid of zone.js because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 52.492,
          "end": 57.42,
          "en": "that Signal feature is a feature provided by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 57.42,
          "end": 60.66,
          "en": "You create signals with that Signal function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 60.66,
          "end": 62.4,
          "en": "that's provided by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 62.4,
          "end": 67.14,
          "en": "and therefore when you change a Signal anywhere",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 67.14,
          "end": 69.223,
          "en": "in your code, no matter if you do it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 69.223,
          "end": 71.82,
          "en": "because a timer expired or",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 71.82,
          "end": 74.898,
          "en": "because a user clicked a button, when you change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 74.898,
          "end": 79.86,
          "en": "a signal's value, Angular of course knows about it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 79.86,
          "end": 81.592,
          "en": "because the Signal is created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 81.592,
          "end": 85.62,
          "en": "with a function that comes from Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 85.62,
          "end": 90.114,
          "en": "So internally, that Signal object that is created here can",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 90.114,
          "end": 95.114,
          "en": "of course notify Angular if it's value changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 95.4,
          "end": 99.926,
          "en": "And the same is true for event bindings, for example, just",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 99.926,
          "end": 103.2,
          "en": "like signals, this is an Angular feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 103.2,
          "end": 107.52000000000001,
          "en": "So of course Angular knows when that button gets clicked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 107.52000000000001,
          "end": 109.8,
          "en": "because it handles the click Event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 109.8,
          "end": 112.74000000000001,
          "en": "it triggers these methods which we set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 112.74000000000001,
          "end": 114.093,
          "en": "with event binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 114.93,
          "end": 118.457,
          "en": "So of course it can still also trigger change detection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 118.457,
          "end": 121.98,
          "en": "for this component without zone.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 121.98,
          "end": 125.88,
          "en": "because it does know about such events.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 125.88,
          "end": 127.172,
          "en": "And therefore with that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 127.172,
          "end": 132.172,
          "en": "in mind, we can actually consider removing zone.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 133.8,
          "end": 138.8,
          "en": "because if we only use signals or event bindings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 139.05,
          "end": 144.05,
          "en": "like this, then in the end we have good sources",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 144.57,
          "end": 147.3,
          "en": "that will tell Angular that something changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 147.3,
          "end": 150.663,
          "en": "and that will allow Angular to run change detection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 151.98,
          "end": 154.195,
          "en": "It's just timers like the one we had",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 154.195,
          "end": 158.875,
          "en": "in the counter variable, which no longer will be considered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 158.875,
          "end": 160.958,
          "en": "because it's timers like these",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 160.958,
          "end": 165.958,
          "en": "that were previously handled by zone.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 166.11,
          "end": 169.05,
          "en": "Zone.js listened to expiring timers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 169.05,
          "end": 171.63,
          "en": "and told Angular that something changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 171.63,
          "end": 175.32,
          "en": "and that Angular should consider running change detection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 175.32,
          "end": 178.86,
          "en": "But if we use signals and we update signals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 178.86,
          "end": 183.36,
          "en": "inside of timers, then we have a way of telling Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 183.36,
          "end": 187.11,
          "en": "that something changed even without zone.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 187.11,
          "end": 190.29,
          "en": "And that's why they offer when using signals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 190.29,
          "end": 193.47,
          "en": "we can get rid of zone.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 193.47,
          "end": 197.7,
          "en": "And it turns out that Angular nowadays when using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 197.7,
          "end": 202.14,
          "en": "at least version 18, allows you to do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 202.14,
          "end": 205.11,
          "en": "And since Angular sets up subscriptions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 205.11,
          "end": 208.5,
          "en": "in the places where you read a Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 208.5,
          "end": 212.7,
          "en": "in your templates, since Angular does that, it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 212.7,
          "end": 217.17000000000002,
          "en": "of course also knows which parts should be checked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 217.17000000000002,
          "end": 221.67000000000002,
          "en": "for changes and which parts of the application should update",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 221.67000000000002,
          "end": 224.57999999999998,
          "en": "as a Signal value changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 224.57999999999998,
          "end": 228.48,
          "en": "And therefore you can actually get rid of zone.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 228.48,
          "end": 231.18,
          "en": "And that in the end of course will lead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 231.18,
          "end": 234.81,
          "en": "to more fine-grained change detection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 234.81,
          "end": 239.7,
          "en": "It leads to a smaller bundle size to a smaller code bundle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 239.7,
          "end": 243.84,
          "en": "that's being produced because the zone.js code isn't part of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 243.84,
          "end": 247.256,
          "en": "that bundle anymore and it leads to less",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 247.256,
          "end": 250.77,
          "en": "behind the scenes checks, less listeners",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 250.77,
          "end": 252.69,
          "en": "for events behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 252.69,
          "end": 256.83,
          "en": "So lots of good things and therefore here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 256.83,
          "end": 258.6,
          "en": "in this application I'll switch back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 258.6,
          "end": 262.8,
          "en": "to using signals by going to the messages service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 262.8,
          "end": 267.8,
          "en": "And here I'll remove that subject and set messages back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 268.052,
          "end": 273.052,
          "en": "to being a Signal, which will manage an array of strings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 274.89,
          "end": 277.33,
          "en": "I'll get rid of the 'rxjs' import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 278.49,
          "end": 281.15999999999997,
          "en": "and I'll get rid of the allMessages() gather",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 281.15999999999997,
          "end": 283.5,
          "en": "and instead set all messages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 283.5,
          "end": 288.183,
          "en": "to this.messages.asReadonly() as it was before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 289.257,
          "end": 293.73,
          "en": "And here in addMessage I'll simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 293.73,
          "end": 297.176,
          "en": "update() my messages Signal with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 297.176,
          "end": 301.71,
          "en": "that update() method where I get the oldMessages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 301.71,
          "end": 305.49,
          "en": "and where I then return a new array which copies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 305.49,
          "end": 307.41,
          "en": "all the old messages into it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 307.41,
          "end": 309.513,
          "en": "and adds the new message at the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 311.94,
          "end": 313.83,
          "en": "In the new message component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 313.83,
          "end": 318.627,
          "en": "I also wanna set enteredText back to being a signal();",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 320.16,
          "end": 322.96,
          "en": "and therefore Signal must be imported here of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 323.94,
          "end": 328.23,
          "en": "and I'll therefore read the value down there where I need it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 328.23,
          "end": 330.7,
          "en": "and I'll reset it by using the set(''); method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 333.12,
          "end": 337.17,
          "en": "and then the MessagesListComponent TypeScript file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 337.17,
          "end": 341.49,
          "en": "I no longer register this property like this anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 341.49,
          "end": 344.28,
          "en": "Instead I just add messages and reach out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 344.28,
          "end": 347.317,
          "en": "to thismessagesService.allMessages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 349.23,
          "end": 352.383,
          "en": "so that I store a reference to that Signal here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 354,
          "end": 357.21,
          "en": "I can get rid of the AsyncPipe import here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 357.21,
          "end": 362.21,
          "en": "and here and then the template instead of using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 362.31,
          "end": 364.56,
          "en": "that AsyncPipe, I now simply read",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 364.56,
          "end": 366.513,
          "en": "that messages Signal again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 368.52,
          "end": 372.06,
          "en": "And with that, this entire app uses Signals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 372.06,
          "end": 375,
          "en": "in all the places where I'm managing data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 375,
          "end": 378.783,
          "en": "that might change, I'm using Signals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 380.97,
          "end": 385.5,
          "en": "As a result we can now get rid of zone.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 385.5,
          "end": 389.37,
          "en": "and we do that in a two step process.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 389.37,
          "end": 392.79,
          "en": "The first step is to go to the angular.json file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 392.79,
          "end": 396.33,
          "en": "which configures this Angular project and how it's built.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 396.33,
          "end": 401.04,
          "en": "And there in the \"build\" node under \"polyfills\",",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 401.04,
          "end": 405.49,
          "en": "you wanna make sure that this zone.js polyfill is removed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 407.7,
          "end": 410.01,
          "en": "and you'll need to stop your development server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 410.01,
          "end": 412.683,
          "en": "and restart it for that to have an effect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 414.69,
          "end": 418.17,
          "en": "In addition, in the main TS file, you should now go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 418.17,
          "end": 420.54,
          "en": "to bootstrapApplication",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 420.54,
          "end": 424.59,
          "en": "and add that configuration object to add providers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 424.59,
          "end": 426.315,
          "en": "and it's now a special provider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 426.315,
          "end": 431.315,
          "en": "that should be imported from '@angular/core'",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 433.538,
          "end": 435.54,
          "en": "and the provider we need here is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 435.54,
          "end": 437.76,
          "en": "the provideExperimentalZonelessChangeDetection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 441.3,
          "end": 444.96,
          "en": "And this provider has this name for a reason.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 444.96,
          "end": 447.93,
          "en": "At the point of time where I'm recording this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 447.93,
          "end": 450.993,
          "en": "it's experimental, it's not stable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 451.92,
          "end": 455.55,
          "en": "It may contain bugs and it's likely to change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 455.55,
          "end": 458.61,
          "en": "The name will also likely change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 458.61,
          "end": 459.727,
          "en": "So if you are watching this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 459.727,
          "end": 462.577,
          "en": "it might already be named provideZonelessChangeDetection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 464.58,
          "end": 467.07,
          "en": "At the moment, it still has that name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 467.07,
          "end": 470.28,
          "en": "And in the end this here is a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 470.28,
          "end": 473.523,
          "en": "which you should execute here in your provider's array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 475.11,
          "end": 480.11,
          "en": "That will now disable zone.js for this Angular application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 480.24,
          "end": 484.68,
          "en": "So now, zone.js won't help Angular detect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 484.68,
          "end": 488.52,
          "en": "whether some timer expired or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 488.52,
          "end": 492.423,
          "en": "Now it really comes down to signals telling Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 492.423,
          "end": 495.423,
          "en": "that something changed and that's it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 496.62,
          "end": 499.95,
          "en": "This also means that in the counter.component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 499.95,
          "end": 502.56,
          "en": "where I opt out of zone.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
